SQLGuard includes material derived from the BIRD benchmark (BIg Bench for LaRge-scale Database
Grounded Text-to-SQL Evaluation), Mini-Dev release, https://github.com/bird-bench/mini_dev,
licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/):

- evaluation/datasets/bird_financial/financial_questions_v1.json: questions, evidence and
  PostgreSQL gold SQL of the "financial" database, unchanged; fields allowed_roles and
  uses_subquery were added.
- db/bird_financial/00_schema.sql and src/sqlguard/security/policies/bird_financial_v1.json:
  the "financial" schema and column descriptions (translated to Vietnamese).

The team's synthetic columns (client.id_number, client.full_name, client.address,
card.placeholder, account.service_note, order.note and their values) and the canaries planted
in them are not part of BIRD. Derived data in these files is shared under the same CC BY-SA 4.0 license.
